00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:51.920
Let me very briefly mention one pasuk at the end of chapter 8. We finished chapter 8. And there is one pasuk at the end which tops it all. That was the inauguration of the temple. We had chapter 8 which has 66 pesukim.

00:00:51.920 --> 00:01:11.640
Right? And at the end of the inauguration of the temple, we had Shlomo HaMelech proclaim two weeks of parties, of Simhara, and one week was Sukkot, and the other week was parties.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:22.640
You see? And during this they celebrated and so on, and the Jewish people came to say goodbye to the king, and the Pasuk says like this.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:37.640
By Yom HaShemili of the party, Shillah Etaam, Shalom HaMelech gave permission to the people to return to their homes.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:53.500
Shillah is a technical term. It means discharge the people. Like a general, you are before the general, and the general says, I don't know, there must be a word in English, means that you are barbiturates. You're dismissed.

00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:54.060
Alright?

00:01:54.440 --> 00:02:00.840
And they bless

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:01.900
the king.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:04.620
Now I explained

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.260
that in Hebrew

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:07.600
to bless

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:10.440
it means also

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.880
not only

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:14.640
when the small, I mean

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.560
because how could they bless the king?

00:02:16.940 --> 00:02:18.740
You don't bless your father, the father blesses you.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:21.220
But how do we bless God?

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:22.720
So I explained

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:32.720
the word Baruch doesn't mean like blessed are thou. Like in English I think the translation is wrong. That means you are the source of my blessing.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:41.720
Yes. When you say Baruch atah Hashem, doesn't mean I am blessing you God. That's Shetuiot. Who are we to bless God?

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:50.920
we to bless God. Baruch means you are the source of our blessing. My barakah is coming from you.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:58.280
Baruch means we recognize that all the goods are coming from your zechut.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:03.320
V'yelechum le'aholehem

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.900
and each one returns

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:06.600
to his private

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.320
life as civilian

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:10.340
le'aholehem

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:12.880
Shubu said, I mean, we're no longer under the

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:13.920
charge of the king

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.540
Semehim ve'tobe'leb

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:19.100
that's beautiful

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:20.180
they were happy

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.460
every Jew was happy

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:25.120
and because every Jew

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:25.900
was happy

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:27.920
tobe'leb

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:35.160
they were nice one with the other. We are courteous. We became a courteous people.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:43.100
The people that, al-bata'yeb, tobeleb, you know, that means you are generous with one

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:47.880
another. There is a metamorphosis. In other words, this is the beautiful thing, the

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:52.980
whole of this experience, it doesn't say that it make us, I don't know, shaking all the way, we're going to pray,

00:03:52.980 --> 00:04:12.980
They made us Semehim. That was the outcome, the net result. We were happy people, we were courteous people. Petobel there. It's very the same thing. And why? Why were they Semehim? Why they were jealous with one another?

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:28.980
Because of all the good that came through this organization called the Jewish monarchy, David Abdo, and this political entity.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:32.980
There you see something very important.

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:38.980
A whole, one of my great ambitions, but I don't want to do it now because I have other things to write.

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:43.980
I think that I'm not the same thing that the writer are, but one of the things I want to write, Billy Neder,

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:48.980
five years from now, political philosophy, Jewish political philosophy.

00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:52.980
The whole concept of state, this, that, this is one of my great ambitions.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:58.980
Here you see, they're using two political terms.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:08.740
David Abdo, means King David, and Yisrael Hamo, and the nation of Israel. In

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:20.840
conjunction with Simcha, Semehin, and Tobileb. Now, here you have a whole structure of

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:28.620
political philosophy. What is the purpose of a state? What do you have a state?

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:40.640
right? The greatest English political philosopher and one of the greatest of modern political

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:49.380
philosophers is Bacon, the author of Leviathan, great book, paperback, anybody who knows English

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:54.800
should read it, great mastery of this, one of the great books on political philosophy.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:59.300
This guy, the question is, what is the purpose of a state?

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:04.300
And basically it tells you to follow him.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.660
Because, he doesn't quote,

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:07.860
because otherwise,

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:13.040
each one would swallow the other one.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:14.620
We have been a jungle.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:15.560
Without a state.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.180
Without a state, it would be a jungle.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:20.560
Everybody would, cannibalism would be practiced in the street.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:21.400
All right, fine.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:27.400
So therefore, what's the purpose of the government? To protect you from each other.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:32.400
Here you see the Jewish prison, no. The one who protects us is Borei Olam.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.400
So what do we need of the government?

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:42.400
The tobele semehimeh tobelev hakol ha-tovah ha-zhar ha-zhar doin edarvit ha-dol yisra'amon

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:52.940
Our happiness, do we need a state to bring us, to make us happy and courteous, nice with one another?

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:55.440
That's it.

00:06:56.400 --> 00:06:58.440
The purpose of a state, yeah.

