I mean, it's not going to be... but he was...

00:36:04.040 --> 00:36:09.040
there's no way, in no way that this guy out of the way was finished.

00:36:09.040 --> 00:36:11.040
But I will tell you something, yes.

00:36:11.040 --> 00:36:14.040
I did not see one Talmud coming from his tahachado that is not a crook.

00:36:14.040 --> 00:36:16.040
All of them are crooks.

00:36:16.040 --> 00:36:19.040
I have no respect for him or his Talmudim.

00:36:19.040 --> 00:36:21.040
That's the simple reason, they're crooks.

00:36:21.040 --> 00:36:29.040
Anyhow, there comes the point, very important.

00:36:29.040 --> 00:36:33.040
If you go before me when David your father went,

00:36:33.040 --> 00:36:36.040
in the presence of his heart and in his heart,

00:36:36.040 --> 00:36:39.040
to do as your father did, your words and your words will be heard.

00:36:39.040 --> 00:36:44.040
And build with me your throne, the throne of Israel for ever.

00:36:44.040 --> 00:37:04.040
My Shekhinah is here forever, God says in the Vitamigdash. Yours not. This place is Kaddosh forever.

00:37:04.040 --> 00:37:16.840
No matter what's going to happen, Darbenaar is going to say, if you destroy the B'edamikdash, still there will be the Bisham Kol HaYamim, the Kedushah will remain there forever.

00:37:16.840 --> 00:37:28.840
Your kingdom, your dynasty, it depends whether you observe the Torah or not.

00:37:28.840 --> 00:37:34.620
If you don't observe the Torah, I'm not going to keep you as a king.

00:37:37.940 --> 00:37:41.900
Now, I want to explain something very important.

00:37:44.740 --> 00:37:52.080
I believe, I never read it someplace, but I would like one day to,

00:37:52.620 --> 00:37:56.720
I hope that somebody wrote a book like this and to sit down and read about it.

00:37:56.720 --> 00:38:06.720
I honestly believe that Shlomo HaMelech, so to speak, was taking a gambling.

00:38:06.720 --> 00:38:11.720
Was a gambler. A gambler. How?

00:38:11.720 --> 00:38:17.720
If there is no Bet HaMikdash, there is no Galut.

00:38:17.720 --> 00:38:25.720
For the first time, we are going to hear about the concept of Galut in this chapter.

00:38:25.720 --> 00:38:27.720
Galut? Galut.

00:38:27.720 --> 00:38:29.720
There is no Beit Beg Daesh? There is no Galut.

00:38:29.720 --> 00:38:31.720
Let me explain to you.

00:38:31.720 --> 00:38:33.720
There is no Beit Beg Daesh.

00:38:33.720 --> 00:38:35.720
Like in time of the Shofritim,

00:38:35.720 --> 00:38:37.720
the story of the Haraz al-Ahad,

00:38:37.720 --> 00:38:39.720
the Haron,

00:38:39.720 --> 00:38:41.720
but this is not a national

00:38:41.720 --> 00:38:43.720
catastrophe.

00:38:45.720 --> 00:38:47.720
Now that you have Beit Beg Daesh,

00:38:49.720 --> 00:38:51.720
and the Shekhinah is with

00:38:51.720 --> 00:38:53.720
us,

00:38:55.720 --> 00:39:02.220
Now, Avon means the end of the political system.

00:39:02.220 --> 00:39:06.800
I'm going to say, the God who destroyed the king will destroy the kingdom.

00:39:06.800 --> 00:39:11.100
And, as you're going to see a few Pesachim later, there will be a Chorvah mit Amikdash,

00:39:11.100 --> 00:39:15.240
and the people will be going to Galut.

00:39:15.240 --> 00:39:18.480
So, here, let me again repeat.

00:39:18.480 --> 00:39:22.380
I believe that's like this. I never saw it within no place.

00:39:22.380 --> 00:39:27.880
I wish, I hope that there is a book with them, the subject, but I did not read it.

00:39:27.880 --> 00:39:31.480
My thesis is a simple thesis.

00:39:31.480 --> 00:39:35.620
If Bola Olam is Yishav Haim and we are on the others,

00:39:35.620 --> 00:39:38.800
yeah, we want to continue.

00:39:38.800 --> 00:39:44.740
Bola Olam is not going to punish us in a miraculous manner.

00:39:44.740 --> 00:39:50.840
But if the Shekhinah is down here on earth, in the Beit HaMikdash,

00:39:50.840 --> 00:39:53.620
Every single Avon counts a lot.

00:39:54.400 --> 00:39:56.200
Just like every single Echud counts a lot.

00:39:57.080 --> 00:39:58.540
The king is in front of you.

00:39:58.680 --> 00:39:59.500
You are with the king.

00:40:00.260 --> 00:40:00.500
Yes?

00:40:00.940 --> 00:40:02.540
And therefore if you offend the king,

00:40:03.180 --> 00:40:04.400
then you pay the consequences.

00:40:05.600 --> 00:40:07.180
This is what he's saying to him here.

00:40:07.840 --> 00:40:08.200
He says,

00:40:08.200 --> 00:40:08.220
He says,

00:40:08.220 --> 00:40:14.220
And you will go before me when David comes to you and tells you to stop all the laws and laws that you have been able to keep

00:40:14.220 --> 00:40:19.220
Then you will establish your kingdom on Israel for ever

00:40:19.220 --> 00:40:22.220
For ever is a condition that you observe all the laws

00:40:22.220 --> 00:40:25.220
When I spoke about David, I told you a lot

00:40:25.220 --> 00:40:28.220
And this is nothing new I am telling you Shlomo

00:40:28.220 --> 00:40:31.220
I already told this to your father David

00:40:31.220 --> 00:40:34.220
No one will take you from the throne of Israel

00:40:34.220 --> 00:40:36.220
However

00:40:36.220 --> 00:40:46.220
If any of you makes a Havon, Teshuvah l'rahah, not the tova, you return to make Havon.

00:40:46.220 --> 00:40:55.220
Yes. Teshuvah means to return. Now, if we are in sin, we return to good. If we are in good, we return to bad.

00:40:55.220 --> 00:41:00.220
If you do not believe, you will be behind me

00:41:00.220 --> 00:41:01.220
You do not follow me

00:41:01.220 --> 00:41:04.220
Specifically what I mean is

00:41:04.220 --> 00:41:07.220
Do not listen to my words, my laws that I gave you

00:41:07.220 --> 00:41:11.220
And you went and followed other people and joined them

00:41:11.220 --> 00:41:14.220
Why is there a verse in the Shema?

00:41:14.220 --> 00:41:18.220
And I made Israel above the earth

00:41:18.220 --> 00:41:20.220
I would spoil the people of Israel

00:41:20.220 --> 00:41:24.220
Now, here is something very interesting

00:41:24.220 --> 00:41:34.220
Normally, if Mr. A makes a Havon, Mr. B should not be punished for it.

00:41:34.220 --> 00:41:42.220
That's not the case here. If the government of Israel makes a Havon, you know who's going to be punished?

00:41:42.220 --> 00:41:48.220
Not the government of Israel. The people. Look what it says here.

00:41:48.220 --> 00:41:56.220
And you have chosen to make a new religion and you have decided to make Israel your own.

00:41:56.220 --> 00:42:02.220
Not Shlomo. Not the sons of Shlomo.

00:42:02.220 --> 00:42:08.220
I'm going to... Why? Because of very simple philosophy.

00:42:08.220 --> 00:42:14.220
Don't tell me the government is the government. You have the power to change it.

00:42:14.220 --> 00:42:16.220
People's choice.

00:42:16.220 --> 00:42:18.220
People's choice.

00:42:18.220 --> 00:42:20.220
Absolutely. Absolutely.

00:42:20.220 --> 00:42:28.220
When they put too much taxes on them, they tell them, get out from here.

00:42:28.220 --> 00:42:34.220
Yes? Too much taxes, they revolt.

00:42:34.220 --> 00:42:36.660
No, it's the Amir goes,

00:42:36.660 --> 00:42:38.740
That's a

00:42:38.740 --> 00:42:40.740
No, that is, what does it mean?

00:42:40.740 --> 00:42:42.740
That's more important.

00:42:42.740 --> 00:42:44.740
How simple is that?

00:42:44.740 --> 00:42:49.420
So in the Jewish mind, it's very important,

00:42:49.420 --> 00:42:51.420
the Rambam has it and so on.

00:42:51.420 --> 00:42:54.940
When the kingdom, when the government sins,

00:42:54.940 --> 00:42:59.180
the people are responsible.

00:42:59.180 --> 00:43:01.180
From our point of view,

00:43:01.180 --> 00:43:09.140
There is no difference between Achman and Mr. Nazi, Mr. German, this, Deutschman.

00:43:10.360 --> 00:43:12.380
Whatever his name happened to be, Mr. Schmidt.

00:43:13.360 --> 00:43:13.700
All right?

